      "lineNbr": 701,
      "author": {
        "id": 26549
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-26T08:59:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Both motion search functions has 2 steps:\n- full-pixel search, which does not understand scaling and requires `av1_get_scaled_ref_frame` to prepare the **scaled** ref frames.\n- sub-pixel search, which understands scaling and search on the raw ref frame.\n\nAnother awkward thing is that motion search routines always look at the 0th slot, so we have to swap the frame we want them to search into that slot.\n\nSo `block_ref_scale_factors` have to be swapped as well or sub-pixel search will see mismatched scale factors.",
      "parentUuid": "2ff5abdc_e0ddcd72",
      "revId": "cbab34c9e12e3c38a57493c6aa04aea4f0154faa",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
